  "body": "## Cause\n\nThe untabbed levels of a 2D Contour start at their own seat (the axis start or the lead-room reseat). The tabbed levels cut windows between the tabs. The first window began after the last tab, not at that seat. So the lead-in of the first tabbed window stood in sheet that no level above cut. The dive fed from the plunge height to the level in one move (`contour_step.rs` `graze`, `descent_dive.rs` `feed_down`).\n\nThe context pack named a second cause: the tabbed levels skip the reseat. On the fixture, the raw start and the reseated start are the same point. That change alone had no effect, and this PR does not make it.\n\n## What changed\n\n- `crates/motion/src/machining2d/tab_clear.rs`: new `level_start`. It returns the untabbed ring, started at the point where window 0 of the tabbed levels begins.\n- `crates/motion/src/machining2d/contour.rs`: the untabbed levels of a tabbed ring use `level_start`. The tab layout does not change.\n- Exception: a ring keeps its old seam if it shares a level with another ring of its band, or with another band of a whole-model contour (`PreparedBand::room`). Two rings that cut the same path must split it at the same seam. Without this exception, the path crossing law blocked the post in `contour_whole_step.rs` case 1 and case 2 (`Crossing { moves: [15, 59] }`).\n- A contour with no tabs, a ring that walks no tabbed level, and a picked start do not change.\n\n## Readings\n\nFixture `crates/motion/tests/contour_tab_entry.rs`:\n- L-shape, Outside, `bottom_z` -18.3, stepdown 4.5, 4 tabs 10 x 3, D6.\n- Plunge entry, Arc lead r3, clearance 25, retract 12.\n\n\"Disc floor\" is the highest floor under the full tool disc that the earlier level passes left. \"Crescent\" is how far the disc reaches past the cut under its centre.\n\nPLANAR links, before (origin/main 44c13a01d):\n\n| level | entry XY | plunge Z | below disc floor | crescent |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| -4.5, -9, -13.5, -15.3 | (43.514, -5.802) | 2 -> level | 4.5, 4.5, 4.5, 1.8 | 0 |\n| -18 window 0 | (46.000, 8.865) | 2 -> -18 | 18.0 | 2.501 |\n| -18 windows 1-3 | (10.153, -6), (-6, 29.525), (21, 30.029) | 12 -> -18 | 18.0 | 2.501 |\n| -18.3 windows 0-3 | as -18 | 2 or 12 -> -18.3 | 0.3 | 0 |\n\nPLANAR links, after:\n\n| level | entry XY | plunge Z | below disc floor | crescent |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| -4.5, -9, -13.5, -15.3 | (46.000, 8.865) | 2 -> level | 4.5, 4.5, 4.5, 1.8 | 0 |\n| -18 window 0 | (46.000, 8.865) | 2 -> -18 | 2.7 | 0 |\n| -18 windows 1-3 | unchanged | 12 -> -18 | 18.0 | 2.501 |\n| -18.3 windows 0-3 | unchanged | 2 or 12 -> -18.3 | 0.3 | 0 |\n\nStay-down ramp preset (`level: KeepDown`, `transition: Ramp`), after: window 0 enters at the untabbed start (46.000, 8.865). The levels below the first do not cut the lead-in, so the disc floor there is -4.5. The dive is 13.5 mm below it, with a 2.501 mm crescent. Before, it was 18.0 mm at (46.000, 8.865) with the untabbed start at (43.514, -5.802).\n\nLead None: every window dives on the ring, 2.7 mm below the tab-top level, before and after. Window 0 now enters at the untabbed start.\n\nTab hops are not changed: a feed rise from the level to Z12, a rapid, and a plunge back to the same level.\n\n## What is not fixed here (scope split by the coordinator)\n\n- Refs #3678 (P3): a guard for a dive deeper than one stepdown below the disc floor. It covers windows 1-3 (18 mm, 2.5 mm crescent) and the stay-down ramp window 0 (13.5 mm). It also covers a ring that keeps its seam by the exception above.\n- Refs #3679: the verifier passes such a plunge with a centre-cutting tool. The issue has the evidence (the reporter's `verify` result and a code read). No verifier law is added in this PR.\n\n## Pins (red first)\n\n`crates/motion/tests/contour_tab_entry.rs`:\n- `the_first_tabbed_window_enters_where_the_levels_above_cut_its_lead_in`\n- `the_first_tabbed_window_of_the_stay_down_ramp_enters_at_the_untabbed_start`\n- `a_tabbed_level_without_a_lead_enters_in_the_kerf_of_the_level_above`\n\nEach test was red on origin/main: window 0 did not enter at the untabbed start. The pinned window 1-3 readings change on purpose with #3678.\n\n## Files that moved\n\n- `examples/catalog/2d/contour-tabs/contour-tabs.nc`: 44 lines. It was regenerated with `cargo xtask catalog --case 2d/contour-tabs`. The Z4 and Z2 levels now lead in at `X51. Y-6.515`, where the Z0 tabbed level enters. Before, they led in at `X38.514 Y-30.802`. The Z0 lines (`G00 X51. Y-6.515 Z8.` / `G01 X51. Y-6.515 Z0. F300`) did not change. Now the two levels above cut that point.\n- `examples/catalog/2d/contour-tabs/contour-tabs.camproj`: the cached toolpath of the same case (348 lines). The open PR #3251 also changes this file. #3251 will need a refresh after this PR merges.\n- No golden moved: `golden_cl`, `conformance` and `first_part_programs` pass with no change.\n\n## Gate (final head, debug, `-j 6`)\n\n- motion: `--lib`, `--no-run`, and these binaries pass: `contour_auto_side`, `contour_inside_ramp`, `contour_outside_floor`, `contour_start`, `contour_start_comp`, `contour_tab_bridge`, `contour_tab_entry`, `contour_tab_height`, `contour_tab_lead`, `contour_tab_necks`, `contour_tabs`, `contour_whole`, `contour_whole_new_outline`, `contour_whole_no_floor`, `control_comp`, `lead_room`, `machining2d`, `pass_start_levels`.\n- app: `--lib`, and these binaries pass: `conformance`, all 13 `contour_*`, `docs_troubleshooting`, `example_catalog`, `example_catalog_adaptive`, `example_catalog_edge_work`, `first_part_programs`, `golden_cl`, `mcp_verify`, `offset_pass_start`, `verify`.\n- `cargo xtask catalog --check`: pass.\n- clippy `-D warnings`: motion `--all-targets`, app `--lib`: clean.\n\n## Not run\n\n- No heavy lane and no light lane (P3).\n- No app window and no reporter file. The q07 project was not opened.\n- No fresh `verify` run of the fixture (see #3679).\n\nEffort: high (no escalation).\n\nChangelog: 2D Contour with tabs: the levels above the tabs now start where the first tab window enters, so that window dives into the cut of the level above and not into uncut sheet.\n\nRefs #3453\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
